## Slow / platform check evidence

**Fast CI passing does not satisfy this section.** Fill one row per selected slow or platform-specific check from `test-routing.yml`. Never report an unrun check as passing: write `not run — <reason>` and link the tracking issue.

| Surface | Command | Result | Evidence |
|---------|---------|--------|----------|
| <!-- e.g. iOS e2e --> | `make check-e2e-ios` | pass (n/n) / fail / not run — reason | run link, log excerpt, or screenshot |
| <!-- e.g. migration replay --> | `make check-migration-replay` | | |

## Test changes

- [ ] New or changed tests are in the right tier (fast/slow) and have a per-test timeout
- [ ] No test was retried, skipped, or disabled outside the quarantine registry (`test-quarantine.json`)
- [ ] Coverage floors in `.standards.yml` (`coverage.minimum` / `coverage.scopes`) still hold; no scope was lowered

## Quarantine (if touched)

<!-- Delete if the registry was not changed. -->

- Entry added/removed:
- Issue:
- For removals: link to the 20x stability run

## Manual verification

<!-- Steps CI cannot reach (device, keychain, production-only). Each one has a tracking issue or a runbook under docs/runbooks/. -->

## Checklist

- [ ] Conventional Commit title
- [ ] Tests written first (TDD) and run on the tested commit above
- [ ] No production host or real identity is reachable from any e2e lane this PR touches
